    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Near the cold storage room, sous-chef Lyova notices that expensive truffles are missing and questions the cooks. Bound by his promise to tell only the truth, Max exposes Senya's hiding spot, forcing Senya to claim he was merely testing security.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "А трюфеля никто не брал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Там не хватает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Луи, ты не видел?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Лавров?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Видел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Где они?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Кто их туда положил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Что такое, Лёв? Спокойно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Просто хотел проверить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Смотрит кто-нибудь тут или нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А то продукты пропадают.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Твои проверки?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "А трюфеля никто не брал?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did nobody take the truffles?' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'and' and finishing on 'took'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Там не хватает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Some are missing there.' The negative particle sits right before the verb meaning 'is enough' to negate the statement.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Луи, ты не видел?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Louis, did you not see them?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'Louis' before landing on 'saw'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Лавров?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Lavrov?' In Russian, the idea of 'proper name' flows naturally into 'proper name' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Видел.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I saw them.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'saw' and finishing on 'saw'. Lyova answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Где они?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where are they?' Lyova anchors the line on 'where', while 'they' completes the thought.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Кто их туда положил?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who put them in there?' The meaning hinges on 'who' working together with 'put' in spoken Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Что такое, Лёв? Спокойно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What is the matter, Lyova? Easy.' In Russian, the idea of 'what' flows naturally into 'calmly' without extra filler words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Просто хотел проверить.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I just wanted to check.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'simply' before landing on 'to check'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Смотрит кто-нибудь тут или нет.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Whether anyone watches things here or not.' Notice how Russian expresses 'looks' and 'no' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "А то продукты пропадают.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Otherwise groceries keep disappearing.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'and' before landing on 'disappear'. Lyova answers right away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "lyova",
      "t": "Твои проверки?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your inspections?' Lyova addresses the listener with the informal singular 'you' alongside 'inspections'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
